## Operator sequence used (forge the forge)

```text
1. Ahmes batch already PROCESSED_OK → extraction.db per PDF
2. athanor inject --from-manifest … --project-slug profield-frontend-pedagogy --library scholar
3. Athanor search  → candidate node_ids (never cite snippets)
4. sqlite / ahmes query <db> --nodes --page N  → read full node
5. ahmes query --cite <db>:<node_id> --style chicago-author-date
6. Insert only evaluator_safe=yes; else [BIBLIO-GAP] + still keep coat·node·page for reopen
```

Many coats still fail the cite gate because host `title` was `Abstract` / `1 INTRODUCTION` / `Keywords` while Crossref has the real work title (`host_registry_mismatch`). That is **12G.4 heading quality** (SHIPPED 2026-08-16 in Ahmes), **not** missing PDFs and **not** a forgotten RIS/`--force-meta` pass (force-meta alone re-selected the bad heading). Do not invent AU/TI. Re-run `enrich --force-meta --online` (or batch `--online`) on coats with a post-12G.4 Ahmes, then re-cite; until then keep explicit `[BIBLIO-GAP]`.
